      "content": "That looks much better, thanks for the clean flow. It actually passed the initial automated check, but the score was a bit on the lower side (the count was pretty low). \n\nThe editor-in-chief wants to make sure these recipes feel \"substantive\" in the layout. Can you try one more version that's a bit more detailed? You don't need to be repetitive or weird about it, just make sure the steps are really comprehensive and the ingredients are well-integrated so the thoroughness score isn't so low. I still really don't want you to just spam the words though, it needs to stay professional.",
