      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To prepare this dish, start by seasoning 4 bone-in, skin-on chicken thighs with salt and pepper, making sure to coat them evenly. In a large skillet, heat a sufficient amount of oil over medium-high heat until it reaches a temperature of around 400°F (200°C). Add the chicken thighs to the skillet and sear them until they achieve a golden-brown color on both sides, about 5-6 minutes per side. Remove the chicken from the pan and set it aside on a plate. Next, add 3-4 cloves of minced garlic to the same skillet and sauté for 1-2 minutes, until fragrant and lightly caramelized. Be careful not to burn the garlic. Finally, pour in 1/2 cup to 3/4 cup of heavy cream, stirring constantly to achieve a thickened sauce. Reduce the heat to medium-low and let the sauce simmer for 2-3 minutes, until it reaches your desired consistency. Serve the chicken over cooked pasta, spooning some of the creamy sauce over the top and garnishing with chopped fresh herbs, if desired.",
