      "content": "To prepare this dish, start by seasoning 4 bone-in, skin-on chicken thighs with salt and pepper, making sure to coat them evenly. In a large skillet, heat a sufficient amount of oil over medium-high heat until it reaches a temperature of around 400°F (200°C), which is ideal for searing the chicken. Add the chicken thighs to the skillet and sear them until they achieve a golden-brown color on both sides, about 5-6 minutes per side, or until they reach an internal temperature of 165°F (74°C). While the chicken is cooking, mince 3-4 cloves of garlic and set it aside. Once the chicken is done, remove it from the pan and set it aside on a plate. Next, add the minced garlic to the same skillet and sauté for 1-2 minutes, until fragrant and lightly caramelized, stirring occasionally to prevent burning. Then, pour in 1/2 cup to 3/4 cup of heavy cream, which will help to create a rich and creamy sauce. Stir the cream into the garlic and let it simmer for 2-3 minutes, until it reaches your desired consistency. Serve the chicken over cooked pasta, spoon",
